{# The language of the pages (issue #448, architecture §5.7): one button per language this deployment
   serves, in a form and with no script, so that it answers a keyboard and a browser that runs nothing.
   The provider keeps the choice for this browser and records it on the journey in progress, which is why
   the interaction travels with it; the language is never in the URL.

   It is for whoever is not known yet (issue #485): somebody who is signed in reads these pages in the
   language their record names and changes it where that record is changed, so there is nothing here to
   offer them and the control is not rendered, as it is not rendered under two languages.

   "data-locale" is what a stylesheet reads, never a class. This is the bare
   version the suite of the integration renders; the application serves its own (apps/beffroi/templates/beffroi/_locale_switcher.html.twig),
   which reads what the kernel of this suite does not boot. #}
{% set locales = beffroi_locale_choice() %}
{% if locales|length > 1 %}
    {% set interaction = app.request.query.get('interaction') %}
    <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_locale') }}" data-locale="choice" aria-label="{{ 'locale.choose'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_locale') }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="target" value="{{ app.request.requestUri }}">
        {% if interaction %}<input type="hidden" name="interaction" value="{{ interaction }}">{% endif %}
        {% for locale in locales %}
            <button type="submit" name="locale" value="{{ locale }}" data-locale="{{ locale }}"{% if locale == app.request.locale %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                {{ ('language.' ~ locale)|trans([], 'beffroi') }}
            </button>
        {% endfor %}
    </form>
{% endif %}
